{
  "coverage": [
    {"reason":"Explains the efficiency and investor-protection purpose; creates no separate approval exemption.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u0.2"},
    {"reason":"Establishes post-authorisation scope and home-supervision context; immediate effect is read with the express Effective Date.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u1.190"},
    {"reason":"Heading identifying the UCITS measures.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u2.523"},
    {"reason":"Introduces the distinct categories of post-authorisation measures.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u3.575"},
    {"reason":"Separate exemption for changes of depository and investment delegates; it does not replace the conditions for investment changes.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u4.653"},
    {"reason":"Provides the investment-change exemption, home-requirements condition, and product-feature and local-policy exceptions.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u5.840"},
    {"reason":"Notification alignment is separate from prior approval; exemption does not eliminate notification requirements.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u6.1221"},
    {"reason":"Identifies relevant FAQs, forms and checklists whose operative details are not supplied.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u7.1419"},
    {"reason":"Heading governing commencement and transition.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u8.1677"},
    {"reason":"Fixes commencement on 2025-11-28.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u9.1696"},
    {"reason":"Preserves the existing process for applications received before commencement and still unapproved or unauthorised at commencement.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u10.1809"},
    {"reason":"Identifies management companies as the audience for continuing obligations.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u11.2030"},
    {"reason":"Preserves SFC post-vetting, enquiries and possible regulatory action even when prior approval is unnecessary.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u12.2069"},
    {"reason":"Identifies relevant SFC case officers as the clarification channel.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u13.2377"},
    {"reason":"Identifies the issuing division.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u14.2489"},
    {"reason":"Identifies the issuing regulator.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u15.2518"},
    {"reason":"Limits UCITS coverage to the listed domiciles and includes UK schemes authorised as UK UCITS.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u17.2556"},
    {"reason":"FAQ reference is supplied, but its contents are absent and remain an unresolved implementation dependency.","status":"UNCERTAIN","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u18.2831"},
    {"reason":"Forms and checklists reference is supplied, but its contents and any relevant procedural requirements are absent.","status":"UNCERTAIN","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u19.2914"}
  ],
  "dimensions": [
    {
      "dimension":"scope",
      "explanation":"The reading concerns material post-authorisation changes to investment objectives, policies or restrictions of the circular's defined UCITS funds. It does not extend the exemption to every fund described elsewhere as UCITS or to initial authorisation.",
      "source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u1.190","d97b56331f41a.u5.840","d97b56331f41a.u17.2556"],
      "status":"PROPOSED"
    },
    {
      "dimension":"definitions",
      "explanation":"Covered funds are UCITS domiciled in France, Luxembourg, Ireland or the Netherlands, and UK-domiciled collective investment schemes authorised as UK UCITS. Materiality, novelty, complexity and possible local policy implications are not defined in the supplied text and require case-specific judgment.",
      "source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u5.840","d97b56331f41a.u17.2556"],
      "status":"AMBIGUOUS"
    },
    {
      "dimension":"exceptions",
      "explanation":"Relief requires compliance with home-jurisdiction requirements. Either novel or complex product features, or possible local policy implications, excludes relief. Pre-effective-date applications still awaiting approval or authorisation remain under the existing process.",
      "source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u5.840","d97b56331f41a.u10.1809"],
      "status":"PROPOSED"
    },
    {
      "dimension":"modality",
      "explanation":"The circular removes a prior-approval requirement conditionally; it does not grant approval, establish licence possession or certify overall compliance. The exceptions preserve prior approval for the described investment changes. Failure of the home-requirements condition establishes no entitlement to this exemption, rather than a means of curing home non-compliance through SFC approval. Notifications and SFC post-vetting remain separate.",
      "source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u5.840","d97b56331f41a.u6.1221","d97b56331f41a.u12.2069"],
      "status":"PROPOSED"
    },
    {
      "dimension":"time",
      "explanation":"The express Effective Date is 2025-11-28, which controls the introductory reference to immediate effect. 'Before' excludes applications received on that date. The proposed transition reading assesses outstanding approval or authorisation at commencement; the text does not expressly specify that assessment instant or address withdrawal and resubmission.",
      "source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u1.190","d97b56331f41a.u9.1696","d97b56331f41a.u10.1809"],
      "status":"AMBIGUOUS"
    },
    {
      "dimension":"dependencies",
      "explanation":"The relevant FAQs, forms and checklists, existing approval process, applicable home-jurisdiction requirements and facts of the proposed change are needed for a final application. The packet lists unresolved dependencies missing.1c25ffdf5c1e10e0297748d5 and missing.79fb54125bb1f35a1d457fad without contents or a mapping to specific references. Their contents are not inferred.",
      "source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u5.840","d97b56331f41a.u7.1419","d97b56331f41a.u10.1809","d97b56331f41a.u18.2831","d97b56331f41a.u19.2914"],
      "status":"AMBIGUOUS"
    }
  ],
  "questions": [
    "What do the relevant FAQs and existing approval process specify about the exceptions and transitional applications?",
    "What home-jurisdiction requirements apply, and does the proposed change satisfy them?",
    "What are the fund's domicile and regulatory status, the proposed change's features and possible local policy implications, and any application's receipt and approval history?"
  ],
  "readings": [
    {
      "assumptions": [
        "The explicit commencement date controls the introductory reference to immediate effect.",
        "Outstanding approval or authorisation for the transition is assessed at the Effective Date.",
        "The formalization represents the exemption stated in the supplied circular; absent FAQs may clarify its application.",
        "No case-specific fact is assumed true or false."
      ],
      "citations": [
        {
          "quote":"Removing the SFC’s requirement on prior approval for material changes in investment objectives, policies and restrictions which comply with the fund’s home jurisdiction requirements, except for changes that involve novel or complex product features and/or which may have local policy implications.",
          "unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u5.840"
        },
        {
          "quote":"The streamlined measures set out in the relevant FAQs will take effect on 28 November 2025 (Effective Date).",
          "unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u9.1696"
        },
        {
          "quote":"Existing applications received by the SFC before the Effective Date for which no approval or authorisation has been granted will be processed by the SFC in accordance with the existing approval or authorisation process.",
          "unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u10.1809"
        },
        {
          "quote":"1 For this circular, UCITS funds means (i) Undertakings for Collective Investment in Transferable Securities (UCITS) domiciled in France, Luxembourg, Ireland and the Netherlands, and (ii) collective investment schemes domiciled in the United Kingdom authorised as UK UCITS.",
          "unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u17.2556"
        },
        {
          "quote":"The SFC will continue to conduct post-vetting of scheme changes (including those not subject to the SFC’s prior approval) and related revised documents filed with the SFC.",
          "unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u12.2069"
        }
      ],
      "distinction":"The result answers: 'Does this change qualify for the circular's removal of prior SFC approval?' It is an exemption-eligibility predicate, not an overall compliance decision. Within scope, true means the stated exemption applies; false means one or more conditions for this exemption fail. False alone does not establish every requirement under the unavailable existing process. Outside scope, the result supplies no conclusion.",
      "family":"exceptions",
      "formalization":{
        "facts":[
          {
            "meaning":"The fund is a UCITS domiciled in France, Luxembourg, Ireland or the Netherlands, or a UK-domiciled collective investment scheme authorised as UK UCITS.",
            "name":"covered_fund",
            "requires_judgment":true,
            "source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u17.2556"],
            "type":"bool",
            "unit":"Boolean"
          },
          {
            "meaning":"The proposal is a material post-authorisation change in the fund's investment objective, policy or restriction.",
            "name":"material_investment_change",
            "requires_judgment":true,
            "source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u1.190","d97b56331f41a.u5.840"],
            "type":"bool",
            "unit":"Boolean"
          },
          {
            "meaning":"Date for which applicability of the circular's removal of prior approval is assessed.",
            "name":"assessment_date",
            "requires_judgment":false,
            "source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u9.1696"],
            "type":"date",
            "unit":"Gregorian calendar date"
          },
          {
            "meaning":"The proposed investment change complies with the applicable requirements of the fund's home jurisdiction.",
            "name":"home_requirements_met",
            "requires_judgment":true,
            "source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u5.840"],
            "type":"bool",
            "unit":"Boolean"
          },
          {
            "meaning":"The change involves novel or complex product features; either characteristic makes this fact true.",
            "name":"novel_or_complex_features",
            "requires_judgment":true,
            "source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u5.840"],
            "type":"bool",
            "unit":"Boolean"
          },
          {
            "meaning":"The change may have local policy implications; actual realised implications are not required.",
            "name":"possible_local_policy_implications",
            "requires_judgment":true,
            "source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u5.840"],
            "type":"bool",
            "unit":"Boolean"
          },
          {
            "meaning":"An application concerning this change was received by the SFC before 2025-11-28 and had not received approval or authorisation at commencement. False includes cases with no such application.",
            "name":"pending_pre_effective_application",
            "requires_judgment":true,
            "source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u10.1809"],
            "type":"bool",
            "unit":"Boolean"
          }
        ],
        "result":"(and home_requirements_met (not novel_or_complex_features) (not possible_local_policy_implications) (not pending_pre_effective_application))",
        "result_type":"bool",
        "scope":"(and covered_fund material_investment_change (>= assessment_date (date 2025-11-28)))"
      },
      "local_id":"reading.1",
      "questions":[
        "How do the FAQs distinguish novel or complex features and possible local policy implications?",
        "Does the transitional process permit withdrawal and resubmission, and when is pending status assessed?"
      ],
      "statement":"[TRUE_IS_SATISFIED] A material post-authorisation investment change qualifies for removal of prior SFC approval from 2025-11-28 if the fund meets the circular's UCITS definition, the change complies with home-jurisdiction requirements, it involves neither novel nor complex product features, it has no possible local policy implications, and it is not covered by the preserved process for outstanding applications received before that date. True means those exemption conditions are satisfied; false means this exemption is unavailable. Thus materiality alone does not require prior approval. The product-feature and local-policy exceptions retain prior approval, while home non-compliance prevents reliance on the exemption. A pending pre-effective-date application continues through the existing process, whose detailed requirements are absent. Fund management companies must still address applicable notifications and filings; the SFC retains post-vetting, enquiry and regulatory-action powers. No particular fund or change can be classified on the supplied facts.",
      "subject":"Eligibility for removal of prior SFC approval for material UCITS investment changes"
    }
  ]
}
